# Reproducible builds: every stylesheet is embedded verbatim by the esbuild text
# loader, so the checkout MUST always carry LF endings — regardless of the
# developer's core.autocrlf setting. The `**` matters: `src/client/*.css` would
# cover only the top-level stylesheet and leave the per-feature ones
# (paperspace/, tasks/) to be checked out as CRLF on Windows, which would bake
# CRLF into lib/client.js and break cross-platform reproducibility.
src/client/**/*.css text eol=lf

# Built artifacts: keep checkout/commit diffs byte-stable on Windows. They are
# committed on purpose (see docs/development.md), and `npm run check:lib`
# compares a fresh build against them — a CRLF checkout would fail that check.
lib/**/*.js text eol=lf
